  "lineage": "Cuban couple-dance rumba subform with the characteristic vacunao symbolic-pursuit-and-evasion choreographic structure, codified 1880s-onward in Havana-and-Matanzas Afro-Cuban barrios out of solar-tenement-courtyard improvised drumming. Built on three-conga interlocking pattern (tumbador low-pulse, tres-dos middle-syncopation, quinto high-improvisation lead), clave 3-2 or 2-3 wood-block timekeeper, and palitos cáscara stick-on-drum-shell pattern. Vocal structure follows decimas Spanish-poetic-form opening (canto), coro-call-and-response chorus, and montuno open-improvisation section. The faster-tempo rumba-columbia and slower-tempo rumba-yambú are the sibling subforms.",
